Mon Oct 26 11:15:19 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.11.0 (upstream tag v0.11.0, 2026-10-25):
  * Editing: Restrict Editing (file commands, user name, read-only and
    comments-only protection), mail merge to any record or a range of
    records, Convert Text to Table keeps inline content, Convert to
    Text asks for the separator, Split Table fixes, Track Changes
    Accept/Reject can move to the next change, AutoFormat of
    *bold*/_italic_, border lines and tables, Tab/Backspace indents
    and Enter twice for headings, field switches (Upper, Lower, Caps,
    DollarText, Hex...) and more fields updated, Read Mode page color.
  * UI: Format Painter pointer, ruler/save/print keep the view,
    status bar names the page in view, comment times in the user's
    time zone, real tabs in dialogs, SmartArt/chart resize handles,
    table-insert grid preview, highlight shortcut, autoscroll
    follows the scroll direction, translated ribbon tooltips.
  * Layout and import/export: many pagination, table, floating-table
    and rendering fixes closer to Word; DOCX East Asian font hints,
    default font size, text-box story sharing, Word 2003 headers and
    notes; ODT, RTF/LaTeX and spreadsheet import fixes.
  * Proofing and languages: Spanish proofing (es-ES, es-MX, es-419,
    es-UY), proofing options for more languages, Turkic Change Case,
    Khmer ligature fix, Romanian translation, interface translations
    from craft-i18n.
  * Hardening: caps and bounds on VML paths, picture memory, mailing
    text, ui_requests queue, .aff alphabets and numeric parsing;
    encrypted DOCX packages now require the data integrity check;
    file.exportPng validates the extension.
  * CLI/MCP: type_text with paragraphs is one command and MCP keeps
    serving when the app is not open yet.
  * Re-vendor with update=true (669 crates, up from 550): craft-libs
    is pinned to a newer rev (adds craft-i18n with the ICU 2.3 data
    and formatting crates, craft-winprint-gdi), plus chrono's
    iana-time-zone and the release tooling's networking and signing
    stack (hyper, rustls, aws-lc-sys, sigstore, quinn, cms/der) that
    only the non-shipped xtask workspace member uses. New licences in
    the tree: aws-lc-sys (ISC/Apache-2.0/MIT/BSD-3-Clause mix),
    webpki-root-certs (CDLA-Permissive-2.0, CA data), colored
    (MPL-2.0, xtask only) and r-efi (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR
    LGPL-2.1-or-later, MIT chosen); none is copyleft that applies to
    the shipped binaries. cargo_vendor's lockfile audit reports no
    RUSTSEC advisories (the cargo_audit service itself is a no-op).
- Update the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-25.
- Skip the new wall-clock test a_document_of_many_paragraphs_lays_out_in_linear_time
  in %check (timing-ratio assertion, failed on an OBS aarch64 worker)
- Also skip a_long_unbreakable_word_lays_out_in_linear_time in %check
  (same wall-clock ratio assertion, 25.7 vs limit 24 on an OBS x86_64 worker)

