Fri Oct 23 06:57:28 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.10.0 (upstream tag v0.10.0, 2026-10-22):
  * Editing: shape fills with gradients and transparency, personal
    templates for File > New, Format Page Numbers, Table of Figures,
    Split Cells, Convert Text to Table, Cell Margins, Drop Cap and
    picture Size dialogs, Insert Caption, Word's Spike, Word 2003
    legacy menu keys, ribbon groups that shrink to fit, Track
    Changes move tracking, printing scaled to another paper size.
  * Rendering and layout: triple and Word-pattern dashed borders,
    radar charts, legacy text effects and form fields, collapsible
    Navigation pane headings, comments in headers, footers, notes
    and text boxes, many pagination and table fixes closer to Word.
  * Import/export: DOCX glossary (building blocks), OpenType
    ligatures, positional tabs, East Asian layout and mixed
    Hebrew/Latin run order; RTF/ODT sections, ODT column widths,
    master-page headers/footers and embedded MathML; RTF East Asian
    code pages, HTML furigana, Markdown reference links; tagged-PDF
    figures; copied equations go on the clipboard as MathML.
  * Proofing and languages: English dialects (en-GB, en-CA,
    en-AU...) flag each other's spellings, German hyphenation,
    Indonesian spelling, ISO 8859-1 Hunspell dictionaries and
    unreadable-dictionary reporting, proofing settings kept across
    restarts; Dutch, Danish, Slovenian and Romanian interfaces.
  * Linux: Flatpak host font folders are scanned, AltGr types
    accented letters instead of opening KeyTips, and saving to a
    GVFS-mounted NAS share no longer fails on a refused mode change.
  * CLI/MCP: wordcraft-cli runs script files, opens password-
    protected Word files with --password and can update fields
    during conversion; MCP open_document takes a password.
  * Hardening (no CVE ids): pipe or device paths no longer hang or
    exhaust memory, tables nest at most 24 deep, image limits are
    checked before allocating, overflow-checked measurements,
    stricter colour, HTML entity and percent-escape parsing;
    date/time conversion now goes through chrono.
  * Many more fixes in 0.9.0 (2026-10-21) and 0.10.0; see
    upstream's release notes for the full lists.
  * Re-vendor with update=true (530 crates): chrono 0.4.45 is the
    only new crate (MIT OR Apache-2.0, std feature only); the rest
    are minor bumps (ICU crates 2.4.0, tokio 1.54.1 and others)
    with unchanged licences. The newly embedded de.pat (hyph-utf8)
    is MIT. License audit finds no new copyleft, License tag
    unchanged; quick-xml stays at 0.41.0 and no ruzstd is vendored.
    cargo_vendor's lockfile audit reports no RUSTSEC advisories
    (the cargo_audit service itself is a no-op in
    obs-service-cargo 7.2.2).
- Update the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-22.
- Legal-Review-Notice: list the embedded hyph-utf8 hyphenation
  patterns (pl/it/de.pat MIT, pt.pat BSD-3-Clause).
- Keep all eight %check skips (their test bodies are unchanged in
  0.10.0) and refresh the comments: upstream CI now tests the whole
  workspace, but with the optional craft-fonts set this build omits.
- Skip four new 0.10.0 tests that fail on the OBS workers (three
  layout assertions needing the optional fonts and one needing a GPU
  adapter)

