Sun Oct 18 17:32:34 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.8.0 (upstream tag v0.8.0, 2026-10-18):
  * Editing: header/footer editing by double-clicking the margin,
    Alt+numpad character codes, F11 full screen, Ctrl+drag object
    copy, tab stops on the ruler, Sort and Formula table dialogs,
    table formulas with cell references.
  * Import/export: password-protected .doc (RC4/XOR), mail merge
    .xls recipients, RTF/ODT tracked changes, DOCX Office 2016
    charts, legacy form fields, PDF Hebrew/Arabic reading order.
  * Proofing: Korean, Swedish, Croatian and Vietnamese interface;
    Russian, Turkish and Czech spelling/grammar; British spellings.
  * Hardening (no CVE ids): hostile-document DoS and link-export
    guards, bounded hostile run lengths and header/footer depth,
    image byte budgets, overflow-checked measurement parsing.
    Crash recovery with unsaved-work offer; CLI --help.
  * Re-vendor with update=true: chardetng 1.0.0, encoding_rs 0.8.42
    (BSD-3-Clause, already in the tag), craft-pdf 0.1.0, arboard
    3.7.0 and combine 4.6.9 (all else MIT or Apache-2.0).
    License audit finds no new copyleft, License tag unchanged.
    No CVEs in the v0.7.0 to v0.8.0 range, and no ruzstd in the
    vendor set (not affected by RUSTSEC-2026-0344).
  * The three 0.7.0 %check skips still match 0.8.0 tests and stay,
    as does the wall-clock layout skip. Four more 0.8.0 tests fail
    identically on both arches in suites upstream CI never runs
    (two layout, two PDF extraction) and are skipped; git-core is
    now a BuildRequires for the xtask asset test that shells out
    to git.

