Tue Oct 13 07:36:16 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.6.1:
  * Tables: select, insert and move with the mouse, resize by dragging
    borders, double-click a border to AutoFit, vertical merges lay out
    as one cell, and the right-click menu offers the table's commands.
  * Layout closer to Word: kerning, automatic paragraph spacing, list
    indents, keep-with-next, column breaks, hidden end-of-cell marks and
    text frames in headers, footers and cells.
  * Paginated Reading Mode, Hide White Space in Print Layout, print
    preview with page range, odd/even, copies and collate, and comments
    in printed and PDF output.
  * Find: Ctrl+F searches in the Navigation pane, Alt+Q opens the "Tell
    me" command search, and Shift+F10 opens the context menu at the caret.
  * Complex scripts: Myanmar, Khmer and Indic shaping, automatic RTL
    paragraph direction while typing, and numeral display modes.
  * Proofing: Portuguese (pt-BR), Polish and Bulgarian hyphenation,
    persistent custom dictionary, and non-English runs are skipped by
    English proofing.
  * New German interface language, improved Spanish and Polish
    translations.
  * DOCX/DOC/ODT: preserve fonts, ink, custom XML stores and complex-script
    formatting on save; .doc import gains pictures, shapes and tab
    stops; ODT import reads page setup from styles.xml; native saves
    protect the original file.
  * New documents follow the system region (A4, centimetres, decimal
    comma outside the US); add fonts at run time; clipboard pictures
    and foreign formatting survive paste on Wayland.
  * MCP: confine file access with --automation-read-root and
    --automation-write-root.
  * Hardening: pictures travel in the reply and exported links keep only
    safe targets (upstream names no CVE id for it; quick-xml stays at
    0.41, so the RUSTSEC-2026-0195 fix is retained).
  * Re-vendored with cargo_vendor update=true (552 crates): new
    wl-clipboard-rs, zbus, wuff, unicode-script and miniz_oxide stacks
    are all MIT/Apache-2.0/Zlib; no new copyleft beyond the declared
    Unicode-3.0, Ubuntu-font-1.0, OFL-1.1 and CC0-1.0 set.
  * Many UI, dark theme, ribbon and accessibility fixes.

