Sun Oct 11 19:26:07 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package, version 0.5.0:
  * Native word processor with a familiar ribbon: styles, tables, track
    changes, references, mail merge, plus Zotero cite-while-you-write.
  * Reads and writes .docx (macros, signatures and charts survive saving),
    imports Word 97-2003 .doc and password-protected documents via
    pure-Rust agile decryption, opens ODT/RTF/HTML/Markdown/LaTeX, exports
    PDF with a text layer.
  * Word equations (OMML) with an editor, charts, SmartArt, text boxes and
    WMF/EMF pictures render instead of being dropped; RTL/Persian support.
  * File dialogs no longer freeze the window on Linux; touchpad scrolling,
    pinch zoom, dark page mode and a system theme following the OS.
  * Headless wordcraft-cli converter and command server with MCP support.
  * Namespace-declaration memory-exhaustion DoS in document XML parsing
    fixed via quick-xml 0.41 (RUSTSEC-2026-0195).
  * Vendored crates carry no copyleft beyond Unicode-3.0 (ICU),
    Ubuntu-font-1.0 (eframe default font) and CC0-1.0 hyphenation data;
    cargo_vendor runs with update=true as upstream ships no vendor tree.
